\ RISC-V emulation using only Copy-Space copy primitives
\ Each RISC-V instruction is expressed as a sequence of bit copies + minimal logic

\ Model:
\ - Registers are 32-bit regions in space
\ - Instruction decode = copying fields (opcode, rd, rs1, rs2, imm)
\ - Execution = copying data between register regions with transformation

\ Example: addi rd, rs1, imm   (as copy sequence)
\ 1. Copy rs1 value to temporary region
\ 2. Copy immediate bits
\ 3. Perform addition via carry-chain copies (simplified)

macro riscv_addi(rd, rs1, imm)
    \ Copy rs1 register bits to ALU input A
    copybits rs1_region ALU_A 32

    \ Copy immediate to ALU input B
    copybits imm_region ALU_B 32

    \ Addition result copied back to rd
    copybits ALU_result rd_region 32
endmacro

\ This is the direction: every RISC-V op becomes a scheduled copy graph
\ Real implementation needs full bit-level adder/subtractor as copy sequences